   "link": null,
   "locked": false,
   "customData": null,
   "text": "The first three come from PyObject_VAR_HEAD, which every variable sized object starts with. Only the last two belong to lists. A struct is a fixed layout, so ob_size is always at the same offset in every object that has one, which is what lets one function read the length of anything.",
